.TH UNBOUND-DASHBOARD 1 "2026-07-31" "unbound-dashboard" "Unbound DNS Dashboard"
.SH NAME
unbound-dashboard \- lightweight real-time visualization dashboard for Unbound DNS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unbound-dashboard
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unbound-dashboard
is a lightweight, single-binary DNS visualization dashboard written in Go
with SQLite storage. It reads DNS query data from Unbound via DNSTap socket
or verbose log file, and serves a real-time web dashboard with Top-N query
and blocked domain statistics.
.PP
The dashboard listens on port 9153 by default and provides both an HTML
dashboard and a JSON API endpoint for monitoring integration.
.SH DATA SOURCE MODES
.B unbound-dashboard
supports two mutually exclusive data source modes. Exactly one must be
specified at startup.
.SS DNSTap mode (recommended)
Uses the DNSTap Frame Streams protocol over a Unix socket. Requires Unbound
compiled with \fB\-\-enable\-dnstap\fR. Provides real-time streaming with
better performance and structured data.
.SS Log file mode
Tails an Unbound verbose log file. Compatible with any Unbound installation
without extra compile options. Requires \fBverbosity: 2\fR and
\fBlog-queries: yes\fR in the Unbound configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " \fR,\fP " \-\-addr " ADDRESS"
HTTP listen address. Default: \fB127.0.0.1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-p " \fR,\fP " \-\-port " PORT"
HTTP listen port. Default: \fB9153\fR.
.TP
.BI \-d " \fR,\fP " \-\-data\-dir " DIR"
Directory for SQLite database storage. Default: \fB/var/lib/unbound\fR.
.TP
.BI \-D " \fR,\fP " \-\-dnstap " PATH"
DNSTap Unix socket path. Mutually exclusive with \fB\-l\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l " \fR,\fP " \-\-log\-file " PATH"
Unbound verbose log file path. Mutually exclusive with \fB\-D\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " \fR,\fP " \-\-ttl " DAYS"
Data retention period in days. The dashboard automatically purges records
older than this value every hour. Default: \fB90\fR. Maximum: 9999.
.TP
.BI \-S " \fR,\fP " \-\-size " MB"
Maximum database file size in megabytes. When exceeded, the oldest records
are purged. Default: \fB200\fR. Maximum: 9999.
.TP
.B \-V "\fR,\fP " \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h "\fR,\fP " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINTS
Once running, the dashboard exposes three HTTP endpoints:
.TP
.B /
HTML visualization dashboard with Top 10 queries and blocked domains.
Auto-refreshes every 5 seconds.
.TP
.B /stats
JSON statistics API. Returns total queries, blocked queries, uptime,
top queried domains, and top blocked domains. Suitable for monitoring
and scripting integration.
.TP
.B /debug
Plain-text runtime debug information, including data source type,
connection path, database location, and the last 5 ingested records.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start with DNSTap socket:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unbound-dashboard \-\-dnstap /var/lib/unbound/dnstap.sock
.fi
.RE
.PP
Start with log file, listen on all interfaces:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unbound-dashboard \-\-log\-file /var/log/unbound.log \-\-addr 0.0.0.0
.fi
.RE
.PP
Query the JSON API:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl \-s http://localhost:9153/stats | jq
.fi
.RE
.SH SYSTEMD SERVICE
A systemd unit file is provided for production deployments. After
installation via the .deb package, enable and start the service:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemctl enable \-\-now unbound\-dashboard
.fi
.RE
.PP
Edit \fB/etc/systemd/system/unbound\-dashboard.service\fR to configure
the data source and other options before starting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/unbound\-dashboard
The dashboard binary.
.TP
.I /var/lib/unbound/dashboard.db
SQLite database (default location).
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/unbound\-dashboard.service
Systemd service unit.
